# tools/ is password-protected in PHP by tools/_auth.php, not here.
#
# This file used to hold HTTP Basic Auth ("AuthUserFile /REPLACE-WITH-
# ABSOLUTE-SERVER-PATH-TO/tools/.htpasswd"). That needed a server-specific
# absolute path edited in by hand, and every full-site upload replaced the
# edited copy with the placeholder again. Apache then couldn't find the
# password file and answered every request here with a generic "500
# Internal Server Error ... misconfiguration" page. The login now checks
# 'tools_password_hash' in includes/config.php, which a site upload never
# touches - see tools/_auth.php.
#
# Deliberately contains no directives: an .htaccess directive a host
# doesn't allow (AllowOverride) is itself a 500 error, so nothing here can
# break this folder.
